        "id": 131015,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-11T21:02:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chaosmancer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/48/1977_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chaosmancer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Pulseglazer wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;phantaskippy wrote:<br><blockquote>There are a lot of villains that you need a lot of impact int he first few rounds or you can get buried. &nbsp;Having one hero draw two makes it really hard to get out of the early nastiness.It's why despite her strength Unity isn't in the same category as a Wraith or Haka, because she needs team members to set the stage for her domination. &nbsp;Not in giving her card play, but in terms of keeping the game winnable until she is ready to roll.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nWhile I don't disagree, who that we have in the core game is that true of?&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;Bomber Blade comes to mind. Not ony can he be brutal for Unity until he flips but you really need to hit him hard and fast.&nbsp;Same with Voss with a H=4-5 or an unlucky draw on Dawn.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Voss at H = 4 or 5 can still allow Unity draw time if the others can fend off the minions.</p>",
