      {
        "id": 131017,
        "name": "kreistor",
        "username": "kreistor",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9e8a1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-13T22:03:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Unity suffers from \"all hero targets\" effects. They tear her bots apart, and few villains lack that capacity.</p><p>I have played a few games with Unity, but she has never been a powerhouse. Her bots are soft, get shredded fast, and with no self-healing, she does not fare well. If specific bots are in play at specific times... maybe. the biggest problem I have is her inability to get Bots into play. She gets locked up needing to destroy equipment, but has none. If the Unity player starts hitting the equipment of other players without permission... Unity would be put in the box for good. It's selfish, not co-op, to hurt friends to strengthen yourself. Maybe I just haven't been lucky enough to see her come out strong, so i will continue to give her a shot. (Whereas I will not give Chrono-ranger another shot, until a better Innate power becomes available to him.)</p><p>With either Omnitron-X or Absozero to help provide sacrificial equipment, she may get powerful... but why do that when Legacy would make both of the other two powerful instead? Legacy can divert the damage that might wreck O-X's components to himself, and his + damage has such an incredible effect on AZ it's hard to name another character that helps AZ more.</p><p>IMO, Unity is B, maybe B-.&nbsp; Chrono-Ranger is F. O-X is A+, AZ is B on his own but A+ with the right team, and Legacy is always an A despite being boring.</p>",
