      {
        "id": 131026,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-14T18:02:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Omnitron-X, bleh. &nbsp;he's great for villains that rely too heavily on ongoings or for just obliterating the environment deck, after that he's solid.</p><p>Crono-Ranger is going to end fights sooner than OX in most games.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It all depends on your playstyle. &nbsp;I find Crono Ranger to be really strong, and O-X is mostly there to give extra card play and destroy ongoing/environment cards. &nbsp;I'd rather have Adept or Tempest than OX.</p><p>O-X is a normal mode stomper, but I rarely play normal.</p><p>He's great with Unity though, Hasty-&gt;Defensive Blast is golden, and Timeshifting Unity is wonderful, I often put those two together vs. the Ennead for a stomp fest.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:06:15.737Z",
