      {
        "id": 131027,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-14T18:30:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My original ultimate 4-player team was Legacy, Tachyon, Omnitron-X and Tempest.</p><p>Omnitron-X and Legacy can tank.</p><p>Tempest and Tachyon and Omnitron-X can deal damage.</p><p>Tempest and Omnitron-X and Legacy can heal.</p><p>Omnitron-X would start with using his base ability to get Legacy set up.&nbsp; Once Legacy was tanky, then he could focus on other people.&nbsp; This team defeated every villain team on the first try except Voss and Akash'bhuta.&nbsp; Akash pulled out all of her \"play limbs\" cards from just one of them entering play.&nbsp; And Voss had a few too many forced deployments at once.</p><p>My new ultimate 4-player team is Argent Adept, The Scholar, Setback and Tachyon.&nbsp; The Scholar goes Mortal Form to Energy x2 and Solid to Liquid x1 (with Bring What You Need in play).&nbsp; He also gives everyone more card draws and plays and more power uses.&nbsp; Argent Adept heals everyone, gives more card plays, and gives more power uses.&nbsp; Setback gives healing, card draws, and power uses.&nbsp; See where this is going?&nbsp; Tachyon brings extra damage cancelation and more card draws.&nbsp; However, most any other hero would work well in Tachyon's spot.&nbsp; Except maybe Legacy.&nbsp; He makes Setback hurt himself too much.</p>",
        "post_number": 33,
        "post_type": 1,
